          "guid": "mttr74g6js7pspvb",
          "message": {
            "text": "The exact counter fixture is byte-stable across the fontconfig memo boundary. Local cache-reset capture retained SHA-256 c55de7c076cbea2032eccbf526c4b60ee050742fc0fd2f1f0e9774094b30c6b1, 84,650 bytes, and 192 digit cells. The attached native Linux x64 evidence compares the pre-change and candidate refs on the same Noble runner: production medians fell from 20.613s to 3.862s cold and from 20.613s to 3.770s warm, while the Linux SVG remained identical at SHA-256 39f796e8271992d72b4d233c8b43ff1c35eb20121d831466d34e429564e8a50f, 88,210 bytes, and 192 digit cells. The instrumented alternating-order pass reduced fc-match launches from 1,742 to 8 cold and from 1,737 to 0 warm.",
            "markdown": "The exact counter fixture is byte-stable across the fontconfig memo boundary. Local cache-reset capture retained SHA-256 c55de7c076cbea2032eccbf526c4b60ee050742fc0fd2f1f0e9774094b30c6b1, 84,650 bytes, and 192 digit cells. The attached native Linux x64 evidence compares the pre-change and candidate refs on the same Noble runner: production medians fell from 20.613s to 3.862s cold and from 20.613s to 3.770s warm, while the Linux SVG remained identical at SHA-256 39f796e8271992d72b4d233c8b43ff1c35eb20121d831466d34e429564e8a50f, 88,210 bytes, and 192 digit cells. The instrumented alternating-order pass reduced fc-match launches from 1,742 to 8 cold and from 1,737 to 0 warm."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/templates/templates.e2e.test.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 309,
                  "endLine": 333,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  it(\"counter reel survives capture — off-canvas digit cells are kept (DM-1532 capture fix)\", async () => {\n    // The odometer strip is taller than the canvas; its off-canvas digit cells\n    // roll into view during the animation. Capture must NOT drop them (they live\n    // in a data-domotion-anim subtree). Pre-fix only ~1 digit/column survived and\n    // the reels rendered blank mid-roll.\n    const out = await renderTemplateToSvg(\n      counterTemplate,\n      { to: 128500, grouping: true, fontSize: 200 },\n      { browser: await getBrowser() },\n    );\n    clearFontResolutionCaches();\n    const coldAgain = await renderTemplateToSvg(\n      counterTemplate,\n      { to: 128500, grouping: true, fontSize: 200 },\n      { browser: await getBrowser() },\n    );\n    expect(coldAgain.svg).toBe(out.svg);\n    expect(out.svg).toMatch(/@keyframes/);\n    // Every reel animation rests at identity (translateY(0)) — the Domotion-safe\n    // shape that avoids the double-transform. (No `translateY(-…)` resting.)\n    expect(out.svg).toMatch(/translateY\\(0/);\n    // Many digit cells present (6 reels, several rolling multiple turns) — far more\n    // than the ~1-per-column that survived before the capture exemption.\n    const digitCells = (out.svg.match(/>[0-9]</g) ?? []).length;\n    expect((coldAgain.svg.match(/>[0-9]</g) ?? []).length).toBe(digitCells);"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
